// Chapter 01 — "Finally, we can be together forever" (Loop 1 / tutorial day)
// Source: Story/Chapter 01 - Finally, we can be together forever (revised).md
//
// TESTER ENTRY POINT: start the dialogue at node  Ch01_Start
//
// Notes for the Unity team:
//  - Node titles are GLOBAL, so everything here is prefixed Ch01_.
//  - Variables are declared in Ch01_Start. If you later move declares into
//    _system/Start.yarn, delete them here (duplicate declares fail to compile).
//  - Custom commands below must be registered in Unity or Yarn Spinner will warn.
//    Each is a hook for a mechanic from the design doc:
//      <<controls_enable>>                       player gains movement + interact prompts
//      <<quest_start "Name" "objective">>        add quest to log
//      <<quest_update "Name" "objective">>       change objective / tick a checkbox
//      <<quest_strike "Name">>                   strike through in the log
//      <<quest_complete "Name">>                 mark finished
//      <<minimap_show>>                          reveal minimap
//      <<minimap_marker "Place">>                move the marker
//      <<npc_interaction_mode "Place">>          free-talk NPCs at a location
//      <<search_mode "Item">>                    crowd-search minigame
//      <<freeze_frame>>                          cutscene freeze
//      <<title_card>>                            show game title
// Write the commands as no-ops first; the dialogue plays without them.

title: Ch01_Start
---
<<declare $ch01_asked_date = false>>
<<declare $ch01_search_place = "">>
<<declare $ch01_quest_gang_lila = false>>
<<declare $ch01_quest_gang_dira = false>>
<<declare $ch01_quest_gang_kirana = false>>
<<declare $ch01_loop_ended = false>>
<<jump Ch01_Prologue>>
===

title: Ch01_Prologue
---
// EXT. SCHOOL PARK — DECEMBER 10 — AFTERNOON (cutscene)
// Played by the Prologue scene's YarnCutscene, which loads the Dorm scene when this node ends.
// Only character lines play; the narration is kept as comments (stage directions).
// The school festival is in full swing. Bazaar stalls line the paths, a band plays on a makeshift stage, and students crowd around game booths, laughing and trading snacks.
// Every corner has something going on. For one afternoon, the school looks like a utopia.
// The camera drifts through the crowd and settles on Anin, standing at the edge of it all.

Anin: What a fun day... I still can't believe the best three years of my life end tomorrow. What's everyone going to do after graduation?

Kirana: There you are! What took you so long?
Lila: I didn't know you could take a nap in the bathroom.
Dira: Okay, enough, you two. Let's go try the gulali from class 1-C.

// The three of them walk ahead, bickering and laughing. Anin hangs back a step and watches them — a sight she will never forget.

Anin: I don't want this to end. I wish I could stay in high school forever.

// All sound cuts out. For one second, the world holds perfectly still.
// Then the noise rushes back. Anin blinks, shakes it off, and hurries after her friends.

// Turn back on once <<title_card>> is registered in Unity (unregistered commands log a warning).
// <<title_card>>
// No jump: the cutscene ends here and loads the Dorm scene, which should start Ch01_Dorm itself.
// <<jump Ch01_Dorm>>
===

title: Ch01_Dorm
---
// INT. GIRLS' DORMITORY — ANIN'S ROOM — MORNING
An alarm blares. Anin's hand gropes out from under the blanket and slaps at the clock until it stops.

Anin: Good morn— ...huh?

Kirana's bed is empty.

Anin: Where's Kirana? There's no way she'd leave without me. Not on graduation day.

<<controls_enable>>
<<quest_start "Graduation Day" "Get ready for the ceremony.">>

// Interactables: alarm clock, Kirana's empty bed, wardrobe, mirror.
// For the tester build the interactables can just call Ch01_Dorm_Done when finished.
<<jump Ch01_Dorm_Done>>
===

title: Ch01_Dorm_Done
---
Anin showers, does her makeup in a rush, and puts on her graduation uniform.
She stops in front of the mirror. For a moment, she just looks at herself. A single tear slides down her cheek before she even notices it. She doesn't know why.

<<quest_update "Graduation Day" "Go to the auditorium.">>
<<minimap_show>>
<<minimap_marker "Auditorium">>
<<jump Ch01_Auditorium>>
===

title: Ch01_Auditorium
---
// INT. AUDITORIUM — MORNING
Anin expects rows of graduates in matching uniforms. Instead, every student around her is in their regular uniform. She is the only one dressed for a graduation.

Anin: Isn't graduation today? Am I still dreaming? Why is everyone in their regular uniform?

Someone sidles up behind her.

Lila: Well, well. Looks like someone couldn't wait to graduate. What are you cosplaying, the season finale of a high school slice-of-life anime?

A few students snicker. Even Lila is looking at her like she's lost it.

Anin: What is going on? What's the date today? Why hasn't the ceremony started?

-> What's the date today?
    <<set $ch01_asked_date to true>>
    Anin: What's the date today?
    Lila: It's still December 10th, dumbass. And we've got a whole festival to enjoy.
-> Isn't today graduation day?
    Anin: Isn't today graduation day?
    Lila: Sure is — for you, apparently. Congrats, you're the only graduate. The rest of us are still stuck on December 10th, dumbass, and we've got a whole festival to enjoy.

Lila: Stop messing around and let's go find Dira and Kirana. We're enjoying this festival together, no excuses!
Lila: Dira's probably in the classroom doing next semester's homework for fun. Lead the way, boss.

<<quest_strike "Graduation Day">>
<<quest_start "Find the Gang" "Lila: found / Dira: ? / Kirana: ?">>
<<set $ch01_quest_gang_lila to true>>

Anin decides she has either lost her mind or is about to. Either way, she follows Lila to their classroom.

<<minimap_marker "Classroom">>
<<jump Ch01_Classroom>>
===

title: Ch01_Classroom
---
// INT. CLASSROOM — MORNING
Dira sits alone by the window, writing something in a notebook. She doesn't look up until Lila bursts through the door.

Lila: DIRAAA! LOOK AT THIS DUMBASS!
Lila: Someone graduated early today. Cum laude, too — for outstanding academic performance.

Dira laughs softly behind her hand, careful not to hurt Anin's feelings.

Dira: Anin, why are you wearing your graduation uniform? Are you really that nervous about graduating?

-> I don't know... I guess I didn't get enough sleep.
    Anin: I don't know... I guess I didn't get enough sleep.
-> I had a really weird dream last night.
    Anin: I had a really weird dream last night.

Dira: Ahaha. I thought Kirana was pranking you. Where is she, by the way?
Lila: That's what we came to ask you. I thought she was with you.
Dira: She asked to borrow my book, then just ran off with it. I have no idea where she is now.

<<set $ch01_quest_gang_dira to true>>
<<quest_update "Find the Gang" "Lila: found / Dira: found / Kirana: ?">>

Anin: Let's look for her at...

-> The cafeteria
    <<set $ch01_search_place to "Cafeteria">>
-> The music room
    <<set $ch01_search_place to "Music Room">>

<<npc_interaction_mode "{$ch01_search_place}">>
// Tester build: the NPC-interaction minigame can call Ch01_Classroom_Done when finished.
<<jump Ch01_Classroom_Done>>
===

title: Ch01_Classroom_Done
---
The girls search for clues until they run into a student who saw Kirana talking with a group in the school park. The three of them hurry over.

<<minimap_marker "School Park">>
<<jump Ch01_SchoolPark>>
===

title: Ch01_SchoolPark
---
// EXT. SCHOOL PARK — LATE MORNING
The park is packed shoulder to shoulder with festival-goers.

Dira: There are way too many people. We'll never find Kirana in this sea of people.
Lila: Not even Moses could part this crowd. C'mon, Anin, use your spider-sense. You two have been glued together for years.
Dira: Let's just look for my book. It's bright red — it should stand out.

<<search_mode "Red book">>
// Tester build: the search minigame can call Ch01_SchoolPark_Found when the book is spotted.
<<jump Ch01_SchoolPark_Found>>
===

title: Ch01_SchoolPark_Found
position: 98,-174
---
Anin weaves through the crowd, looking for Kirana — or anything that might lead to her. Then she spots it: a flash of red. Someone is holding Dira's book.

Anin: There you are! Where have you b—?!

The student turns around. It isn't Kirana.

Bookworm Student: Oh, hey, Anin. What's up?

The three of them freeze.

Dira: Sorry! We thought you were Kirana, since you have my book.
Bookworm Student: Oh, it's yours? Kirana gave it to me. She said she has a copy of this one somewhere in her room.

-> She doesn't even read her school books.
    Anin: She doesn't even read her school books.
-> There is zero literature in her room.
    Anin: There is zero literature in her room.
-> If she ever read a book, the world would end tomorrow.
    Anin: If she ever read a book, the world would end tomorrow.

Anin: So where is she now?
Bookworm Student: She left right after she gave me the book. Maybe check the photography club? I saw her talking to someone with a camera.
Anin: Thanks.

<<minimap_marker "Photography Club">>
<<jump Ch01_PhotoClub>>
===

title: Ch01_PhotoClub
position: 306,-200
---
// INT. PHOTOGRAPHY CLUB ROOM — NOON
The room is cluttered with props and backdrops, with a few photo sessions running at once. It's quieter here. The first thing they see is Kirana, posing in front of the photo backdrop.

Lila: KIRANUY! We've been looking all over for you!

Lila sprints over — and lands squarely in the frame just as the club member snaps the shutter.

Kirana: You ruined my photoshoot!
Lila: I made your photo a thousand times prettier. Also — behold. The graduate.

-> Call me Anin-senpai from now on.
    Anin: Call me Anin-senpai from now on.
-> You'll have to find a new roommate tomorrow.
    Anin: You'll have to find a new roommate tomorrow.

Kirana bursts out laughing.

Kirana: Okay, but seriously — why are you dressed like that?

-> It's your fault for leaving without me.
    Anin: It's your fault for leaving without me.
-> If only someone had woken me up this morning.
    Anin: If only someone had woken me up this morning.

Kirana: Sorry, sorry! I couldn't wait to see what everyone was doing for the festival. So what's the plan? Just wander around and have fun?
Lila: I mean, yeah, that's the plan. But first, a group photo. Who knows when we'll get another chance to be photographed by the greatest photographer in the world?

Lila shoots the club member a look.

<<set $ch01_quest_gang_kirana to true>>
<<quest_complete "Find the Gang">>

Photography Club Member: Okay. Everyone say "cheese."

The four of them squeeze into the frame. The shutter clicks.

<<freeze_frame>>
<<jump Ch01_EndOfLoop1>>
===

title: Ch01_EndOfLoop1
position: 321,96
---
Lila was right. There would never be a better time than right now — because time itself had broken.
Tomorrow would come, and it would still be December 10th, the day before graduation. So would the day after that, and the day after that — for Anin and for everyone at school.
The girls spent the rest of the day wandering the festival, and that night they slept soundly, ready for whatever tomorrow would — or wouldn't — bring.

<<set $ch01_loop_ended to true>>
// END OF LOOP 1
===
